          "hideComponent": "false",
          "rightMargin": "3",
          "jcr:created": "Thu Sep 10 2020 13:09:36 GMT+0000",
          "gradientDirection": "left-to-right",
          "text": "<h1><span style=\"color: #ffb500;\"><span class=\"futura-bold\"><span class=\"fontsize-1-5em\">EmpowerED to Care: Safe Patient Handling and Nurse Protection in the ED</span></span></span></h1>\n<p><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\">Nurse safety is often discussed at a high level – across entire hospitals or the profession. This course will focus on the unique safety risks nurses face in the Emergency Department, including the cost of unsafe environments. Participants will review recommendations for safe patient handling, violence prevention and explore best practices and technologies that help support nurse safety in the ED.</span></p>\n<p><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\"><b>Learning objectives</b></span></p>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\">Identify the distinct safety risks nurses face in the ED</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\">The cost of unsafe environments</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\">Recommendations for safe patient handling and violence prevention <span style=\"white-space: nowrap;\">in the ED</span></span></li>\n<li><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\">Best practices and technology to help support nurse safety</span></li>\n</ul>\n",
          "jcr:lastModified": "Thu Apr 09 2026 13:59:02 GMT+0000",
          "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/text",
          "rightPadding": "2",
          "backgroundColor": "rgba(255,255,255,0)",
          "textIsRich": "true"
        }
      }
    },
